\begin{theorem}
Different antiself adjoint operators $G\mathbf{\left(  \mathbf{\eta}\right)
}$ map into the same geminal $\left\vert g\right\rangle $ and conversely the
geminal $\left\vert g\right\rangle $ is mapped into different antiself adjoint
operators $G\mathbf{\left(  \mathbf{\eta}\right)  }$ i.e. the correspondence
is not injective i.e.
\begin{equation}
\ker\left(  \mathcal{\Xi}_{\left\vert VV\right\rangle }^{-1}\right)  \neq\phi.
\end{equation}

\end{theorem}

